  "conclusion": "Increasing the old planner from 28 to 70 slices progressively removes radix-step work but cannot cut the primary-input-to-step-31 path before the loop. By 67 slices, 82.43 percent of the combinational path is the invariant pre-step divide-by-zero compare/select; 70 slices adds 1,135 cells and changes timing by exactly zero. At the 73-slice fallback knee the MUX finally receives two legal near-edge slices, the pre-step cone disappears from the winning path, capacitance violations fall from three to zero, and fmax jumps to 224.31 MHz. The final trim then finds a different 66-slice placement at 184.35 MHz, demonstrating non-monotonic placement geometry rather than a simple slice-count curve. Both met points remain outside the 48-slice acceptance limit; selecting operation boundaries earlier and/or flattening before ABC is required."
